  "tag": "fr-FR",
  "label": "France",
  "standard": "Standard European French as a teacher in Lyon or Paris would publish it: neutral, correct, not slangy. Questions with est-ce que or rising intonation; inversion only in fixed polite requests (Pouvez-vous… ?). ne is always written in negatives. France vocabulary for meals and objects.",
